            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for a sweet-maker, then the Gujarati for to sell well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: નગર",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "નગર — nagar — \"a town; a city (formal)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "આ નગર નદીના કિનારે છે. ā nagar nadīnā kināre che. This town is on the bank of the river."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "નગર (nagar) is a tatsama, Sanskrit nagara, \"a town, a city\" (Monier-Williams); it ends many place names."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
